      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2009-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Twenty percent less than \\(60\\) is \\(\\dfrac45\\cdot60=48.\\)\n\nIf \\(n\\) is the unknown number, one-third more than \\(n\\) is \\(\\dfrac43 n,\\) so \\[ \\dfrac43 n=48 \\]\\[ n=36. \\]\n\nThus, the correct answer is D.",
